<h2>Conditions and safeguards</h2>
<p>The bail comes hedged with conditions designed for a witness-sensitive case: no contact, direct or indirect, with the complainant, prosecution witnesses or the deceased's family; no inducement, threat or tampering; residence and mobile-number disclosure; monthly reporting to the SHO on the first Monday of each month; and no travel beyond Delhi without the trial court's leave. The order records that any breach entitles the State to seek cancellation, and that nothing in it reflects on the merits, which the trial court will decide uninfluenced.</p>
<div class="note">For accused persons in long custody, the practical takeaway is to document three things precisely: the custody period from the jail nominal roll, the witness-examination scorecard, and any co-accused bail orders. Those three data points — not rhetoric — moved this application.</div>
